From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristjan Sillmann <kristjan.h.s@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:45:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] se-isinff-bridge

my-vector: vic-anim "SeAssert: se_lib/nrgainv.c:191" (then SIGILL) on some restarts.
libsignalessence_softfp.a is soft-float ABI; nrgainv.o called hard-float glibc __isinff
and policy_actions.o called sin with no math_abi_bridge.o wrapper, so libm read the
argument from a VFP register the caller never set. nrgainv's isinf on the gain-table
ratio could then miss +inf and run past the 18-entry table (NaN gain, assert).

Archive edit (SDK 6.0.0-r08 binutils, ar D):
  objcopy --redefine-sym __isinff=__se_isinff nrgainv.o
  objcopy --redefine-sym sin=__se_sin policy_actions.o
  math_abi_bridge.c + __se_isinff, __se_sin; .o rebuilt with SDK clang 20.1.8
  -O2 -g -march=armv7-a -mthumb -mfpu=neon-vfpv4 -mfloat-abi=hard (same code,
  relocations and ABI attributes as the shipped .o for the old functions)
  the archive's two identical math_abi_bridge.o members collapse to one.
---
 .../build/libsignalessence_softfp.a           | Bin 2632696 -> 2626526 bytes
 .../build/math_abi_bridge.c                   |   5 +++++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/3rd/signalEssence/v009/vicos-highres/platform/anki_victor_example/build/libsignalessence_softfp.a b/3rd/signalEssence/v009/vicos-highres/platform/anki_victor_example/build/libsignalessence_softfp.a
index ffee9404b46cdb4af3c7b257f51ac962b9c03e9b..a086ba9ba3a738572f758328926c694982b2bcbc 100644
